    "body": "## DUNCAN PRIME / SALVADOR — MANGA STUDY -> PRODUCTION KEYFRAME INTEGRATION R01\n\nSOURCE_OF_TRUTH = current #248 + main `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nSTUDIO_HEAD = `f67fd9454a6c2702e60b270634d934dc2ea62665`\nPRODUCT_GOAL = animated film / episode\nREFERENCE_USE = transferable production principles only; NO style cloning / NO panel copying\n\nOWNER supplied JoJo Part 3 Vol.14-17 study material plus a Bleach close-up acting reference. Transferable principles extracted for ZORR:\n- `POSE SILHOUETTE FIRST`: one dominant body gesture must read before internal anatomy/detail;\n- `EXTREME -> QUIET`: high-information action pose should be followed/preceded by calmer staging, not constant maximum noise;\n- `FACE AS ACTION KEY`: close-up acting can function as a major key drawing through asymmetric eyes/mouth, hard value grouping and minimal background;\n- `FORESHORTENING = STORY PRESSURE`: use perspective exaggeration only when the dramatic job is attack/threat/reveal, never as random camera prestige;\n- `BACKGROUND DROPOUT`: at peak impact, environment may collapse into a simple value/motion field so silhouette/effect dominate;\n- `LARGE VALUE MASSES > MICRODETAIL`: face/costume/FX hierarchy must read before hatch/detail;\n- `COUNTERPOSE`: torso, pelvis, head and limb vectors should oppose/offset rather than align as one stiff axis;\n- `IMPACT IS A KEY, NOT SMEAR`: contact/decision frame gets a strong readable shape; motion in-betweens support it.\n\n### Convert #248 witnesses into actual film-ready key drawings\nDo NOT make six technical mannequin sheets. Each witness should also be a reusable cinematic key pose.\n\n**W01 ARM_RAISE — HERO DOMINANCE KEY / CURRENT ONLY**\n- waist-up or 3/4 framing with the raised arm creating a strong negative-space wedge around head/shoulder;\n- face remains the first read; controlled asymmetry in eyes/mouth is allowed when consistent with Duncan identity;\n- shoulder seam + sleeve cap + collar/lapel root must remain visibly attached;\n- armpit compression localized; opposite jacket/lapel/front remains calm;\n- background simple/dark enough that ivory/black silhouette reads immediately;\n- no extreme lens distortion until identity and garment mechanics survive the pose.\n\n**W02 ELBOW_90 — GUARD / HAND-TO-FACE ACTING KEY**\nUse the elbow closure to create a strong hand/face relationship; cuff/watch become readable acting geometry, not technical annotation.\n\n**W03 TORSO_TWIST — TURN-BACK / REVEAL KEY**\nRibcage and pelvis counter-rotate; head finishes the turn. One side compresses, the opposite becomes a long quiet tension plane. Suitable for reveal/decision beats.\n\n**W04 SEATED_COMPRESSION — QUIET MENACE / CONTROL KEY**\nLow-energy pose with strong psychological weight. Let posture, negative space and face do the work; garment compression stays only at hip/waist/hem force zones.\n\n**W05 KNEE_BEND — LANDING / PRE-LAUNCH KEY**\nCompact silhouette, clear center of mass, one compressed leg region and one cleaner opposing plane. This is the key before explosive extension, not a wrinkle study.\n\n**W06 STRIDE_ANKLE — APPROACH / WALKING DOMINANCE KEY**\nLong directional silhouette and asymmetric planted-vs-swing leg treatment. Planted ankle gets the trouser break; swing leg stays cleaner.\n\n### Current legal production order\n`W01 CINEMATIC KEY -> W01 MATRIX QC -> only after valid W01, W02`\n\nW01 must satisfy the existing #248 mechanics matrix AND read as a real anime-film key drawing. No new infrastructure, no technical-sheet detour, no W02..W06 execution before W01 is valid.\n\nSTATE = STUDY INTEGRATED / PRODUCTION DESIGN DELTA RECORDED / W01 STILL NOT PASS",
